   Better, easier idea:  Add staircases with multiple flights.  So a stairway
that went from say, the third level to the 7th level would have "landings" on
intervening levels -- basically a one (or two) square room with no exits that
contains both a stairway up and a stairway down (use two squares only if one
can't put both an up and a down stairway on the same square -- one square would
make more logical sense and only showing the down (or up) stairway would be
good enough as the one square room would be a giveaway.)

  This would allow one to go back up if you went down and got to a landing.
You could also teleport or dig your way out of a landing to that level.  With
magic mapping you could find all the landings on a particular level, so that if
you get to them you have access to many staircases.

  I can forsee some potential problems: 1) if a monster somehow gets created
on a landing it can block the staircase and you can't kill it (except by
digging).  2) Tame dogs (or other creatures) could cause similar problems.
3) If there are more then a few such staircase, the space they take up on a
level could be a problem.  Making the landings bigger would solve all but the
space problem.  Maybe get rid of the walls -- just surround them by 'rock'
(blank space).

  Just thoughts...

